When a click is beside an editing host, on non-editable content around
it, Ladybird focuses nothing in it, and puts the caret before or after
a block-level host rather than inside it. Blink, WebKit and Gecko all
pick the element a mousedown focuses by walking up from the clicked
element: Blink in MouseEventManager::HandleMouseFocus(), WebKit in
EventHandler::dispatchMouseEvent(), and Gecko in EventStateManager::
PostHandleEvent(). None looks for an editor inside it. And Blink’s and
WebKit’s positionForPointRespectingEditingBoundaries() give a point
beside a block child of different editability a position before or
after that child, so the selection only focuses an editor (through
FrameSelection::SetFocusedNodeIfNeeded() in Blink, and FrameSelection::
setFocusedElementIfNeeded() in WebKit) when the point is on its line.
WebKit’s editing/selection/click-outside-editable-div.html test checks
that a click in the padding outside an editable div focuses nothing.
